==Trivia==
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Tank Cat costs 500 [[XP Function|XP]] to unlock instead of 0.
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.4 Update|Version 2.0.4]] reduced Eraser Cat's base health from 1,200 to 800 and base attack from 6 to 4.
**[[Version 2.2 Update#Version 2.2.3 Update|Version 2.2.3]] further reduced Eraser Cat's base health from 800 to 600; Tank Cat is now one of the three [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] to not have its HP doubled in [[True Form]], the others being [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]] and [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline]].
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Wall Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Cat Army MkII (Removed Combo)|Cat Army MkII]] and [[Maxed Out (Removed Combo)|Maxed Out]].
*Tank Cat is the only Normal Cat that has a mouth similar to those of the [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Cats]].
**In part of the trailer for [[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou]], Tank Cat the same mouth as the other Normal Cats.
*Eraser Cat's logo "NEKO" is most likely a reference to the eraser company in Japan, "MONO", while having the word for "Cat" instead.
*In the Taiwanese version, Eraser Cat does not have "NEKO" on its wrapper. The same also applies to [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]].
*The "Really Good™ Defense" stated in Eraser Cat's description may be a reference to the American school supplies manufacturer ''Really Good Stuff''.
*In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], Tank Cat and Eraser Cat have different descriptions, with Tank Cat being regarded as female and Eraser Cat only being strong enough to move a small rock instead of two.
*Tank Cat's description has a typo; it says "with '''the''' great health".
*Prior to [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]], Tank Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Tank Cat
Tough. High health. (Area Attack)
Strong enough to move a pebble. </pre>
<pre>Wall Cat
Rigid defense. Now with corners (Area Attack)
Strong enough to move a small rock.</pre>
<pre>Eraser Cat
Can take a beating thanks to elasticity.
Really Good ™ Defense. (Area Attack)
Strong enough to move two small rocks.</pre>

